    "texture_page_state": "E1 loads DWORD+4 and updates only A8E6F4=(value&0x1f), A8E6F8=(value>>5)&3, and A8E6FC=((value&0x180)==0x180); it does not write A909FC. AC60 selects A909FC later on textured primitive paths from 0x96e6e0 or 0xa6e6e0; these immediate base operands occur at 0xadcb, 0xadd9, 0xaedb, 0xaee9, 0xafec, 0xaffa, 0xb070, 0xb086. Names/ownership remain inferred from behavior.",
    "geometry_and_pixel_workspace": "0xa909b0..0xa90a10; AC60 stages sign-extended coordinates, shifted UV bytes, packet color, texture page, and sprite extents for the software rasterizers.",
